Very first time I did random selection.  Got a Elven Priest with
nothing special in inventory.

Mines entrance on Dlvl2, and the mines weren't dark.  I got to level 3
before I felt confident in gnomebashing and made for Minetown.  Picked
up Mithril armor and Gauntlets of power along the way, and was able to
scrape up enough zm for 2 AC of Divine protection at the Minetown
Temple.  Nothing good at any shop, though!  Took a peak below Mintown
to find an arch lich (from polytrap). No MR on hand, so I went back up
to Dungeons of Doom.

I swapped the mace out for a unicorn horn and got skilled in it.
Price ID'd just about every scroll in the game.  Found =oSD on 2nd
level of Sokoban and  got "oR at the top.

CLOSE CALL 1
Found altar at Dlvl 13 and began sacrificing for artifacts.
Stormbringer on first try!  Accidentally whacked aligned priest with
bloodthirsty Stormbringer and got Jubilex summoned & engulfed/
sickened.  Narrowly escaped via wand of digging and unicorn horn.
Stormbringer kept as alternate weapon from then on.

Lucky Throne sit got wish #1, which got me GDSM.  Back to the mines.

Mine's End was the winecellar.  Got a luckstone and spellbook of charm
monster (which turned out to be the best item this game), but still no
BoH.  Picked up two =oGainCon (each at -1), so I decided to try drain
for gain in "oR Elbereth closet in Sokoban using Stormbringer.  My HP
had been constantly low, and I've never tried HP boosting before in
any game.  I think this ruined my ability to gain skill in Broadsword,
so Stormbringer increasingly became useless.  Genocided L and ; with
found scrolls

CLOSE CALL 2
Finally found BoH and Cursed ?oG on Medusa stage.  Spotted a lonely
nurse on one of the islands so I decided to nurse dance.  Stupidly, I
forgot to burn Elbereth beforehand, resulting in a surprise air
elemental engulfment.  With 22 HP left, I risked pulling a /oT out of
BoH and got a shot off.  Having been killed by numerous air elementals
in the past, I vowed to get more HP and some artifact to halve their
damage.

Found magic lamp; wished for magic marker.  All scrolls but destroy
armor known.  I never did see one of those the entire game.

Got to castle, which I cleared with a boulder fort and my +1 unicorn
horn.  Nothing good in treasure rooms other than GoD.  Used /oW to get
speed boots and Master Key of Thievery.  Wasted a wish trying for the
latter.  Recharged wand and wished up Mjollnir (finally something
better than a unicorn horn!).  It blasts me, but I never let it out of
my hand for the rest of the game. Wand at (0:0)

Gained stealth intrinsic whilst praying for holy water.  Tried
polypiling for the hell of it and got another magic marker.  Found yet
ANOTHER magic marker on part one of the Quest (seriously, Priests get
the best quest with all those chests and wraiths, and it's a joke to
do if you have stealth.  Why do undead sleep anyway?).  Got the Mitre
and leveled to 17 from all the Wraith corpses.

Used all those magic markers to write more ?oCharging, ?oEnchantAmor
and others.  Got really genocide happy and started just hosing stuff
that annoyed me like mind flayers, mimics and trolls.  Did alchemy to
get ~15 blessed potions of full healing, bringing me to ~300 HP.  I
laughed at minotaurs and air elementals.  AC at -37, everything
fireproofed (had to use enchant armors because still no destroy
armors), slow digestion and levitation.  Overkill, right?  It's a good
thing I overprepared...

CLOSE CALL 3
Demogorgon, Yeenoghu and Orcus showed up out of nowhere in one of the
mazes.  Thank you, bones pile.  I had plenty of MR but forwent
reflection in favor of an "oLS I found.  Demogorgon stung me and
brought me down to half HP before I could react, Orcus started
squeezing off death rays, and Yeenoghu fried my =oConflict, =ofSD and
emergency /oFire with a /oLightning.  I escaped up stairs, healed
illness and got out another /oFire.  Fuming, I descended the stairs,
burned Elbereth, and sodomized the lot of them with my +7 Mjollnir.
Bastards.

Replaced lost =oSD with Orcus Town.  Most monsters met in the mazes of
madness just got made into pets with Charm Monster.  Conflict only
used on the Zoo before Rodney and the bottleneck in Moloch's sanctum.

Mysterious Force was very kind to me (hooray Chaotic).  I knew the RNG
would fix that with lots of Archons, but that turned out not the be
the case!

Rodney only showed up twice on way to the planes.  He instead cursed
my inventory about 4 times, but I'm a Priest, so piece of cake.

Earth uneventful as always.  Air (always the hardest plane for me)
dominated by air elems but NO Archons!  Every A.E. that got near me
was made into a pet, which became hilarious after I built an army of
them.  I got 6 of them into plane of fire, who covered me while I
tiptoed to the portal.  Nothing in water but water elementals and
cobras, many of whom became pets, too :)

Astral.  My first time here.  In the past, I always died on Air or
Fire.  Reverse genocided purple worms and zapped them (along with my
angel and last air elemental) with /oTeleport.  Chose the Famine
route, though he was dead before I even opened the door.  I don't know
if worms can eat riders, or my angel/elemental got in some lucky hits,
but oh well!  First altar I saw turned out to be mine, and since I was
still unscathed, I decided to dick around on the altar trying to wrest
one last wish out of my (0:0) wand.  Any monster that got near was
made my pet.  After ~50 zappings, I wished for a blessed figurine of a
woodchuck, but it instantly got killed by a pet Umber Hulk and eaten
by a pet soldier ant...

such rotten luck, right?

